--- a function answering a map whose values can fail (`map[keys, values]`
--- of `float[…]`), called with an argument that can fail: the call's
--- failure is a map of values that can fail, as the function answers it —
--- compiled, its placeholder had been a map of plain floats, and the call
--- site did not build (Rosetta Code, Associative array/Merging)

fn pick[s]
    return map[['a'], [float[s]]]

s = json['"2.5"']
log[pick[s]]
t = json['"x"']
log[pick[t]]
v = json['oops']
log[pick[v].ok]
